{"id":"troupe","lemma":"troupe","pos":"noun","rank":2022,"glosses":["troop"],"ipa":"/tʁup/","audio":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/transcoded/3/3c/Fr-troupe.ogg/Fr-troupe.ogg.mp3","gender":"f","forms":{"plural":"troupes"},"examples":[{"text":"Les troupes avaient beaucoup de bras.","en":"The troops had plenty of arms.","words":[{"g":"the / them","l":"le"},null,{"g":"to have","l":"avoir"},{"g":"much, very much, a lot"},{"g":"of / from"},{"g":"arm"}]},{"text":"Il a décidé de quitter la troupe.","en":"He's decided to leave the company.","words":[{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"has","l":"avoir"},{"g":"to decide","l":"décider"},{"g":"of / from"},{"g":"to leave, to quit"},{"g":"the / her"},null]},{"text":"Les troupes avaient plein d'armes.","en":"The troops had plenty of arms.","words":[{"g":"the / them","l":"le"},null,{"g":"to have","l":"avoir"},{"g":"full, full up"},{"g":"of / from"},{"g":"weapon","l":"arme"}]},{"text":"Nos troupes attaquèrent l'ennemi.","en":"Our troops engaged with the enemy.","words":[{"g":"our","l":"notre"},null,{"g":"to attack","l":"attaquer"},{"g":"the / it"},{"g":"enemy"}]},{"text":"Je pense qu'il nous faut plus de troupes.","en":"I think we need more troops.","words":[{"g":"I"},{"g":"to think","l":"penser"},{"g":"that / what"},{"g":"he / it"},{"g":"we / us"},{"g":"to need","l":"falloir"},{"g":"more / no longer"},{"g":"of / from"},null]}]}